A||||30||FieroHeather||Usefulness of Fiero Passengers||||1||
Z||000000||FieroHeather||09-03-2001||01:27 PM||||Ok, I wanna know something...<P>Are Fiero Passengers only good for being cup-holders??  According to this thread:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003160.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003160.html</A>   Spideyman made an offhand comment in the O/T section about us Fiero Passengers<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by spideyfoot:<BR><B>They must have cupholders or Songman wouldnt go. I guess thats what you call a passenger in a Fiero. A cupholder</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think Im much more useful in a Fiero than holding the driver's drink!  I am a great DJ, co-navigator, and neck messager.  And yes, I am an excellent driver too.  I have only had the privilage of driving a Fiero TWICE in my life (wrote down both dates).  But I think we Fiero Passengers have been getting a bad rep.<P>What's up with that?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>------------------<BR>~A Proud Fiero Passenger~||||reg||1
Z||000001||86seyellow||09-03-2001||01:54 PM||||My Passengers are very important to me&gt;<P>Changes CDS.<BR>Opens my drinks<BR>Argues with me on our directions.<BR>Lights my cigarettes <P>my passenger has never massaged my neck but has given great H/J's<P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||09-03-2001||07:34 PM||||Im not sure 86 yellow but I thing ppl around here would prefer if that off color comments like that are left off the forum just my opinion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||09-03-2001||07:45 PM||||Well Heather, I don't know how much support you are going to get here, there is not exactly an overwhealming number of "passenger" members.  Though, I will say that in the abscense of a passenger I am usually holding drinks in my lap (spilling in the process), scrambling for c.d.s, unwrapping my own chocolate bars, etc...<BR>Oh ya, and carrying conversations alone.  I hate to think what other people are saying when they look over and I'm chewing the fat all by myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHeather||09-03-2001||08:09 PM||||I know that there are not a lot of Fiero Passengers on this forum (Im one of the lucky ones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ), but I do know that you guys occasionally have sidekicks with ya when you are driving.<P>What I want to know is do you just label them "cupholders" or do they have a purpose other than that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000005||KRMFiero||09-03-2001||08:35 PM||||the job of my passanger is to tell everyone in school about when we go sidewayz and airborn and stuff without a lisence, gets alot of people in the school thinking Fieros are awsome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 V-8/Overdrive Tranny<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White) 5 speed with blown clutch :(<P>         <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AOL: Physcokyle     AGE: 15||||reg||6
Z||000006||Standard||09-03-2001||08:35 PM||||I think they make pretty good cupholders.  Passengers don't touch the music  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brian87egotrip||09-03-2001||08:40 PM||||Darn good blind spot checkers. Also good for running into the store to pay for gas and get a drink so they can hold it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||09-03-2001||08:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>I think they make pretty good cupholders.  Passengers don't touch the music   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats exactly the role my passengers take. Don't touch the music, and hold this mt.dew.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||09-03-2001||09:59 PM||||They make good balast in an autocross or track event.<P>Make sure their weight , plus the weight of the battery equals your weight ..or close to it (haha)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroMaster88||09-03-2001||11:09 PM||||I dont know what you guys are talkin bout!  My passangers are good when the car needs a push  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Anything else is left up to me! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||09-03-2001||11:48 PM||||Whats a passenger?<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000012||MsBeth||09-03-2001||11:57 PM||||Heather,<P>I too am a "passenger" and I love it - I have driven fieros in the past but my very short legs don't reach all the way to the clutch or the gas - not without an extender <BR>so it is very uncomfortable. (my sciatica doesn't help either) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>So being driven is actually more fun for me - I love the way the car sounds and how great the ride is!  I plan on being a "professional passenger" which btw guys does not include holding anything, tuning anything, paying for gas or fetching soda, lighting cigs or anything else ... my job is to enjoy the ride,  oh and getting to sit on Mr Mikes leather seats doesn't hurt either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blue_2.gif">  <P>MsBeth||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||09-04-2001||12:01 AM||||Neck massager?!  Come on over!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>We can even take turns driving, no really!<P>Seriously, I just love taking people for rides in the Fiero, I feel like I have a duty to spread the enjoyment of the car around, to do anything less would be selfish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS: you're (Fiero Passengers) are also good for ballast, even up the l/r weight dist. so both wheels break under heeeavy accell   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHeather:<BR><B>Ok, I wanna know something...<P>Are Fiero Passengers only good for being cup-holders??  According to this thread:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003160.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003160.html</A>   Spideyman made an offhand comment in the O/T section about us Fiero Passengers<P> I think Im much more useful in a Fiero than holding the driver's drink!  I am a great DJ, co-navigator, and neck messager.  And yes, I am an excellent driver too.  I have only had the privilage of driving a Fiero TWICE in my life (wrote down both dates).  But I think we Fiero Passengers have been getting a bad rep.<P>What's up with that?!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000014||sloth85GT||09-04-2001||12:15 AM||||Lately my passenger has been my stinky hockey bag, it doesn't say much, and it can't hold my drink. And forget about carrying on a conversation.........<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||09-04-2001||07:40 AM||||I agree with slammed, holds car down in right handers,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If its a girl, lots more fun to play with than radio.||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroHeather||09-04-2001||10:16 PM||||Wow!  I actually found another official Passenger on here!! Woohoo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks MsBeth!<P>I really like riding in the Fiero, for it is low to the ground, handles corners pretty well (compared to my parent's mini-van) and I love being the "lookout" person.  I lookout for people eyeing up the car and I lookout for cops/firetrucks/ambulances for you cannot hear them over the engine/exhaust modifications in some people's cars, or over their radios.  But most of all, I love how enjoyable the ride can be.  Of course you are not snuggled up to the driver--but you have your own piece/section of the car to spread out in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I give darn good neck/back/head/shoulder messages, especially while being the passenger--it is just something I love to do  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>This is all coming from the P.O.V. from one who is not the driver in the Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And thankyou for the offer Ben to let me drive your car--that would rock!  Too bad Im on the other side of the continent dude!!<P>And Im also glad that we passengers can be good for something--even if we add extra weight to the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000017||StuGood||09-05-2001||10:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brian87egotrip:<BR><B>Darn good blind spot checkers... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Absolutely!  And gas station spotters, freeway exit finders, well, whoever said navigator probably said it best.  Plus, if we're in "her territory," and it's rush hour, she gets to drive.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000018||LVMY88||09-05-2001||07:54 PM||||I am also a passenger, though part time now that I have my own Fiero to drive.<BR>When Steve first got his 84SE and made it show ready those many moons ago, we went all over with it. I loved riding everywhere with him in that awesome Fiero. We had so much fun. It's great taking both of ours now, but once in a while it's fun to jump in one of his and go for a drive or to a show.<BR>The Spindles show is a great example. That show falls on our anniversary and was one of the big ones we went to way back with his Fiero1. I decided to ride with him again this year to Spindles as an anniversary of an anniversary of sorts. He fixed the Fiero up including some extra special touches for the show. It was just like old times.<P>Marian<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Marianssig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by LVMY88 (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000019||jelly2m8||09-05-2001||08:00 PM||||Passangers are great when you have that speedo needle pegged, and need some pics takin!!<BR> <A HREF="http://medlem.tripodnet.nu/need4speed/class7-1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://medlem.tripodnet.nu/need4speed/class7-1.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||StansGT||09-05-2001||08:01 PM||||Uhhh, Passengers just add to much weight. I need to go faster, and faster, and faster, and so on!||||reg||3
Z||000021||Lady Pegasus||09-05-2001||09:22 PM||||Hello, my name is Paula and I am a Fiero Passenger.  If I'm lucky, I can some days call myself a Fiero Driver....but seeing as my honey just got the Fiero painted (and also since I got a new toy)...that won't be for awhile.  And hey, the cupholder thing.  87 bought one that fits over the console in the middle.  So NO "cupholding" here.  I just sit back, control the tunes, and enjoy the ride.  (Unless I'm behind the wheel.  Then I'm an anal maniac.  Especially when my honeys nails are diggin' into the dash.  That CAN'T be good for the finish!!!)      <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||4
Z||000022||wkayl||09-06-2001||09:25 AM||||Here is a picture taken by a passenger (me).  It was the first time my daughter ever drove a car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driving_1.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000023||Raydar||09-06-2001||09:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B>Passangers are great when you have that speedo needle pegged, and need some pics takin!!<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Judging by your handle, I'm guessing you slipped in a "ringer".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Not bad!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
